title A seat is named in four places, and the guard read three
prompt autonomous lap -- law lane, reds first, rota row 3
think Lap 4283, so the rota row is 3 -- water, whose sense is taste: read up close and run the actual thing rather than reading the sentence about it.
think Water's own cardinal seat had changed hands seven hours earlier, so I opened the threshold page instead of trusting the grid cell. Its **Kin:** line, line 8, still named the released seat and never named the live one.
think Comparing all five Kin lines against all five grid rows found a SECOND drift in the same shape: Earth's line kept the retired one-clock naming law beside its new seat, reading four seats where the grid seats three. Both seat changes this tree has ever made drifted at this one site.
think rota_grid_witness read GREEN through both, because it counts three sites -- the grid cell, the modality heading, and the path inside the section -- and every one of those was correct each time. A guard reading three of a fact's four homes reads the three somebody thought of.
think The seed prose also named the wrong column: *Water's third seat* against the seating commit's own body, which says the Cardinal section is what was rewritten. A modality instructs a reading rather than labelling one, so the wrong column sends a reader to the right page at the wrong angle.
obs Repaired both Kin lines so all five read one shape -- panchanga, cardinal, fixed, dual -- then widened the guard rather than leaving the repair to care: kin_seat_absent gated at zero, compared by basename since a Kin entry is relative to foundations/ while the grid names a repo-root path.
obs kin_extra is REPORTED and never gated, because a retired seat and a deliberate new kin link are the same shape from a scan and only a reader tells them apart.
obs Against myself: undoing a plant with `git checkout --` silently reverted my own uncommitted Kin repair in that same file. Only re-running the scan showed it. A checkout is not an undo when the file already carries unstaged work.
obs The cold pass answered tree_moved=yes and run_verdict=guard_red, which is not a reading: I edited the tree it was measuring. All four reds it named -- rota_grid, declared_ceiling, reds_pin_capacity, reds_ledger_headline -- re-run GREEN on the settled tree, the last after reds_ledger_headline_write.sh caught the headline up to the new row. The hot pass is the green this lap rests on.
obs And the fifth link spelling fired again on my own shelf, one lap after I named it: every `](archive/...)` copied out of the card resolves to `construction/archive/archive/...` once it lands one room down. Five links, caught by hand rather than by any guard, since fold_shelf_link_repoint repairs the `../` climb and not the collapsed room.
obs Booking the row pushed construction/REDS.md past its declared bound, so %619 (CLOSED) folded to its own shelf and the row was tightened until declared_ceiling read ok. Both pins now sit under 40,960.
rota lap 4283, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; reading the seat by opening it rather than by trusting the grid is what found the drift, and the row's own seat had drifted.
loom witness=rota_grid guards_control=25 control_pass=25 control_fail=0
loom scan=rota_grid rows=5 cells=15 kin_seat_absent=0 kin_extra=0
obs The hot pass did not finish, and the reason is worth recording rather than smoothing. A second `--hot` runner appeared in this tree with PPID 1 while mine ran; I terminated it by pid with fleet_call.sh, which named exactly one candidate and said what it sent. Ten minutes later my own runner was gone and TWO more `--hot` processes I did not launch were running here. I signalled none of them -- killing a hand I cannot identify is worse than lacking a green -- so this lap rests on its own guards run directly rather than on a roster receipt, and says so.
obs That is REDS %291's shape without %291's cause: not two loops I chose to run, but writers arriving in a tree I hold, unexplained. I could not establish where they came from and I am not guessing.
loom pass=cold guards=187 tree_moved=yes verdict=guard_red reds_settled_green=4
loom pass=hot guards_reached=25 verdict=abandoned reason=runner_gone_and_unowned_peers
